---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY, getApp } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('sortie')!;
const effectiveDate = 'August 23, 2026';
const policyVersion = '1.0';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy - ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="How Sortie handles local campaign data and optional Apple Game Center achievements on iPhone."
  path="/sortie/privacy"
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/sortie.png"
  socialImageAlt="Sortie app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/sortie">&larr; {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Version {policyVersion} - Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains how {COMPANY.name} ("we", "us") handles information
      in {app.name}, an iPhone-only, portrait pre-release game for iOS 14 or
      later.
    </p>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>The short version.</strong> {app.name} keeps campaign progress,
      records, and settings in a local JSON save inside the app's container. It
      has no Nintek account, login, cloud-save service, or gameplay backend.
      Apple Game Center is optional and is used only for achievements.
    </p>

    <h2>Information Nintek receives</h2>
    <p>
      The {app.name} app does not send your player profile, campaign progress,
      level records, settings, or Game Center identity to {COMPANY.name}. If you
      email us, we receive the address and information you choose to include so
      we can respond. The app does not automatically attach its local save or
      your Apple Account information to a support message.
    </p>

    <h2>Data stored on your iPhone</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} stores completed campaign progress, per-level wins, best times
      and play counts, total and flawless wins, and gameplay, audio, haptic, and
      text-size settings in a local JSON file. The file remains in the app's
      container on your iPhone. {app.name} does not implement account-based or
      app-level cloud sync, and {COMPANY.name} does not receive a server copy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apple may include app data in a device backup according to the backup
      settings and services you control. Those backups are operated by Apple,
      not by {COMPANY.name}.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Apple Game Center</h2>
    <p>
      When Game Center is available and enabled for your Apple Account,
      {app.name} can authenticate the local Game Center player and report
      achievement progress. The current integration does not use leaderboards,
      and the full campaign remains playable without Game Center.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apple handles the Game Center player name, identifier, achievements, and
      related profile activity under Apple's terms and privacy practices.
      {COMPANY.name} does not operate the Game Center account system or receive
      your Apple Account password.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/iphone/set-up-your-game-center-profile-iphd26b2beaa/ios">
        Apple: set up and manage a Game Center profile
      </a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> - </span>
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising, analytics, and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} has no ads and sends no analytics or tracking data to
      {COMPANY.name}. The current iOS privacy manifest declares no tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Local game data remains on an iPhone until {app.name} changes it or you
      delete the app. Deleting {app.name} removes its local save from that
      iPhone. Because there is no Nintek account or gameplay backend,
      {COMPANY.name} cannot retrieve, restore, or delete a server copy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting {app.name} does not delete your Apple Account, Game Center
      profile, or Apple-held achievement records. Use Apple's Game Center and
      privacy controls to manage information held by Apple.
    </p>

    <h2>Children and regional privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} is a general-audience strategy game. It does not knowingly send
      a child's personal information or gameplay to a Nintek service. Apple's
      age, family, consent, and account controls apply when a child uses Game
      Center.
    </p>
    <p>
      Privacy laws in your region may provide rights over personal information
      a business holds. {COMPANY.name} does not hold {app.name} gameplay or
      Game Center account data. Contact us if you believe we hold personal
      information in support correspondence.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy if {app.name}, its Apple service integrations,
      or our data practices change. The version and effective date above
      identify the policy currently published for {app.name}.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or information you sent to {COMPANY.name}?
      Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
      For help using {app.name}, visit
      <a href={app.supportPath}>Sortie Support</a>. Use of Sortie is subject to
      the <a href={app.termsPath}>Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
